      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f0f37e7f28e74047f4179c6|full_name}: I think the 3rd-party server will discontinue to maintain or break is a problem, but won’t be critical problem. because author of world  should maintain their world regularly, or they might can't support some user (eg. PC-only world, which quest user can't get in). \nI think the discontinue or out-of-maintain will be very usually, because most of world author is volunteer, so may be disappear for one month with no expected just because busy on school or work, so a work around is telling authors, that author should make a mock image or content for if the server is going down, and avoid breaking the user experience.",
      "viewerReactions": null
